1
00:00:34,701 --> 00:00:36,703
‎STEEL BALL RUN
‎JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE

2
00:01:52,237 --> 00:01:54,488
‎What's this?

3
00:01:54,489 --> 00:01:56,491
‎#08
‎TUSK, PART 2

4
00:02:20,223 --> 00:02:23,851
‎My nails... shot out...

5
00:02:23,852 --> 00:02:26,104
‎from my paralyzed feet...

6
00:02:26,646 --> 00:02:29,190
‎My nails shot out!

7
00:02:31,401 --> 00:02:34,611
‎Is this thing causing this?

8
00:02:34,612 --> 00:02:38,908
‎What's going on?
‎Did this thing just save me?

9
00:02:42,787 --> 00:02:44,831
‎What the hell are you?

10
00:02:53,339 --> 00:02:55,675
‎It's back in my arm!

11
00:02:56,384 --> 00:02:57,594
‎It wrote something.

12
00:02:58,386 --> 00:02:59,929
‎What's this?

13
00:03:02,307 --> 00:03:04,142
‎That thing has a will of its own.

14
00:03:04,976 --> 00:03:06,895
‎It definitely does!

15
00:03:07,687 --> 00:03:11,773
‎My legs won't move now,
‎but they did when my nails shot out.

16
00:03:11,774 --> 00:03:14,902
‎Did that thing draw something out of me?

17
00:03:14,903 --> 00:03:16,236
‎That thing just now...

18
00:03:16,237 --> 00:03:19,698
‎And these letters... They aren't English.

19
00:03:19,699 --> 00:03:21,910
‎Nothing about this makes any sense.

20
00:03:22,952 --> 00:03:26,205
‎The terrorists' objective...
‎Gyro's homeland...

21
00:03:26,748 --> 00:03:27,874
‎And...

22
00:03:28,708 --> 00:03:32,086
‎Why is that thing attached to me?

23
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:39,135
‎There's more...
‎It isn't just this left arm.

24
00:03:40,094 --> 00:03:43,598
‎There are other mummified body parts...

25
00:03:44,098 --> 00:03:46,184
‎Together, they form a whole body!

26
00:03:47,018 --> 00:03:51,648
‎Someone's corpse has been torn apart
‎and scattered across this land.

27
00:03:52,732 --> 00:03:55,275
‎That's what the terrorists are after!

28
00:03:55,276 --> 00:03:58,488
‎They're using
‎the Steel Ball Run race to find it!

29
00:03:59,072 --> 00:04:02,991
‎If I got all of them,

30
00:04:02,992 --> 00:04:05,954
‎I'd gain even more power.

31
00:04:08,665 --> 00:04:11,960
‎That's Gyro's other Steel Ball.

32
00:04:16,839 --> 00:04:19,132
‎Damn it!

33
00:04:19,133 --> 00:04:21,511
‎One, two...

34
00:04:22,845 --> 00:04:24,430
‎Three!

35
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:29,936
‎Ka-clang! Three of my teeth are busted!

36
00:04:32,146 --> 00:04:34,481
‎I wonder if teeth are any good to eat.

37
00:04:34,482 --> 00:04:37,025
‎Probably not something you can eat.

38
00:04:37,026 --> 00:04:40,028
‎Damn!
‎I had no idea it was this powerful.

39
00:04:40,029 --> 00:04:42,489
‎That guy... What was his name again?

40
00:04:42,490 --> 00:04:45,033
‎Jyohnee Jeoshter.

41
00:04:45,034 --> 00:04:48,870
‎But now I know where he's hiding it.

42
00:04:48,871 --> 00:04:51,331
‎It's in his left arm.

43
00:04:51,332 --> 00:04:54,668
‎He's not carrying it.
‎It's attached to him.

44
00:04:54,669 --> 00:04:58,255
‎The corpse
‎is inside Jyohnee Jeoshter's arm.

45
00:04:58,256 --> 00:05:01,967
‎Which means my search is over.

46
00:05:01,968 --> 00:05:06,723
‎I can just kill Jeoshter first,
‎then take it!

47
00:05:09,350 --> 00:05:12,269
‎Where'd that bastard go?

48
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:13,563
‎That's strange.

49
00:05:14,397 --> 00:05:17,066
‎He's gone!

50
00:05:23,114 --> 00:05:26,908
‎What the hell? Where'd he go?

51
00:05:26,909 --> 00:05:30,997
‎No way. Even if he could run,
‎he couldn't have gotten far.

52
00:05:37,837 --> 00:05:41,466
‎Hey, old man. Are you awake?

53
00:05:48,598 --> 00:05:51,017
‎Did you do that with your leg?

54
00:05:51,976 --> 00:05:53,101
‎Ka-clang.

55
00:05:53,102 --> 00:05:54,812
‎In all that confusion,

56
00:05:55,396 --> 00:05:59,484
‎you slipped the Steel Ball off my plate
‎and over to Jeoshter.

57
00:05:59,984 --> 00:06:01,485
‎But...

58
00:06:01,486 --> 00:06:03,653
‎Now this is getting good!

59
00:06:03,654 --> 00:06:05,447
‎There are two possibilities.

60
00:06:05,448 --> 00:06:10,619
‎Either those grooves were signaling
‎Jeoshter to run the other way,

61
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:16,625
‎or you were telling him
‎to come this way instead.

62
00:06:16,626 --> 00:06:18,835
‎You really are interesting.

63
00:06:18,836 --> 00:06:21,630
‎I'll let you live, Gyro Zeppeli.

64
00:06:21,631 --> 00:06:26,094
‎At least until I find Jyohnee Jeoshter!

65
00:06:48,199 --> 00:06:49,658
‎Damn!

66
00:06:49,659 --> 00:06:52,453
‎He's nowhere! Absolutely nowhere!

67
00:06:54,622 --> 00:06:55,873
‎Ka-clang!

68
00:06:56,415 --> 00:07:00,252
‎This is so damn interesting,
‎but I've got no idea how he's doing it!

69
00:07:00,253 --> 00:07:03,672
‎Is he hiding underground?

70
00:07:03,673 --> 00:07:07,051
‎All I know is he's hiding somewhere.

71
00:07:09,929 --> 00:07:11,973
‎Lick, lick! Damn you!

72
00:07:12,557 --> 00:07:16,185
‎Where'd you go, Jeoshter?

73
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:20,314
‎Just as I thought.

74
00:07:20,815 --> 00:07:24,944
‎They can only see
‎and attack from directly above.

75
00:07:25,611 --> 00:07:27,697
‎They've completely lost track of me.

76
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:31,950
‎But one thing's become clear.

77
00:07:31,951 --> 00:07:34,703
‎No matter who Gyro is or what his goal is,

78
00:07:34,704 --> 00:07:37,415
‎he's a good guy.

79
00:07:38,166 --> 00:07:42,002
‎He used his Steel Ball to show me
‎where the enemy was.

80
00:07:42,003 --> 00:07:44,464
‎He must've done it against all odds!

81
00:07:44,964 --> 00:07:47,300
‎I could even use that to get away.

82
00:07:48,384 --> 00:07:52,013
‎But I'm never giving up the corpse!

83
00:07:52,889 --> 00:07:54,681
‎This has become my hope.

84
00:07:54,682 --> 00:07:58,936
‎And Gyro gave me the courage
‎to face the future I'd given up on!

85
00:07:59,437 --> 00:08:02,063
‎I know where you are now, Gyro!

86
00:08:02,064 --> 00:08:04,275
‎I'm heading for those rock formations!

87
00:08:09,739 --> 00:08:11,449
‎Slow Dancer!

88
00:08:16,746 --> 00:08:18,663
‎All right!

89
00:08:18,664 --> 00:08:21,750
‎I'll give him back to you, Jeoshter!

90
00:08:21,751 --> 00:08:24,670
‎You can have your horse back.

91
00:08:25,838 --> 00:08:27,088
‎Ka-clang.

92
00:08:27,089 --> 00:08:29,132
‎Horses are smart. They sense things.

93
00:08:29,133 --> 00:08:30,800
‎It smells you or hears you.

94
00:08:30,801 --> 00:08:34,972
‎Maybe it wants to get back
‎to its owner, huh?

95
00:08:35,723 --> 00:08:39,310
‎This is bad.
‎Slow Dancer's looking for me.

96
00:08:44,273 --> 00:08:47,026
‎Well, well. Did you find him?

97
00:08:50,154 --> 00:08:53,533
‎No, Slow Dancer!
‎Please, go the other way!

98
00:08:56,911 --> 00:08:59,330
‎What's this? This smells like...

99
00:09:05,044 --> 00:09:06,921
‎What?

100
00:09:09,131 --> 00:09:11,049
‎Underground after all!

101
00:09:11,050 --> 00:09:14,052
‎Come on out and show yourself.

102
00:09:14,053 --> 00:09:18,181
‎I'll tear you apart with my hooks
‎right after I roast you a little.

103
00:09:18,182 --> 00:09:21,310
‎Before the heat reaches inside your arm!

104
00:09:25,398 --> 00:09:27,108
‎There you are!

105
00:09:28,317 --> 00:09:32,154
‎This is the end! Take this, Jeoshter!

106
00:09:37,159 --> 00:09:38,411
‎Wood?

107
00:09:40,246 --> 00:09:41,956
‎I carved it out of deadwood.

108
00:09:43,207 --> 00:09:47,169
‎This has gone beyond a nail.
‎It's a tusk.

109
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:50,172
‎From now on, I'll call it Tusk!

110
00:10:08,232 --> 00:10:10,860
‎I did it. I really did it.

111
00:10:11,861 --> 00:10:13,613
‎Me of all people.

112
00:10:24,749 --> 00:10:25,875
‎Gyro...

113
00:10:26,459 --> 00:10:29,211
‎Gyro? You're okay, aren't you?

114
00:10:30,254 --> 00:10:32,797
‎In this Steel Ball Run race,

115
00:10:32,798 --> 00:10:35,216
‎I can't trust the competitors,
‎Steven Steel,

116
00:10:35,217 --> 00:10:38,179
‎the sponsors... anyone.

117
00:10:38,763 --> 00:10:40,056
‎Except Gyro.

118
00:10:40,598 --> 00:10:42,766
‎He's the only one I can trust.

119
00:10:42,767 --> 00:10:45,102
‎I want your thoughts on the corpse!

120
00:10:45,728 --> 00:10:48,313
‎Are you breathing, Gyro?

121
00:10:48,314 --> 00:10:49,856
‎Wake up!

122
00:10:49,857 --> 00:10:52,233
‎Where do you keep that stitching thread?

123
00:10:52,234 --> 00:10:53,444
‎Where's the thread?

124
00:11:00,993 --> 00:11:02,661
‎What?

125
00:11:02,662 --> 00:11:04,704
‎Gotcha!

126
00:11:04,705 --> 00:11:08,041
‎That was my bait, Jeoshter!

127
00:11:08,042 --> 00:11:11,295
‎I used Gyro himself as bait!

128
00:11:13,297 --> 00:11:14,965
‎Ka-clang!

129
00:11:16,467 --> 00:11:18,885
‎That's exactly why I kept Gyro alive!

130
00:11:18,886 --> 00:11:21,347
‎You pathetic little weakling!

131
00:11:22,765 --> 00:11:24,349
‎-Johnny?
‎-Gyro!

132
00:11:24,350 --> 00:11:28,311
‎Looks like I won, Jeoshter!

133
00:11:28,312 --> 00:11:31,315
‎Go right through Gyro
‎and come straight to me!

134
00:11:33,984 --> 00:11:35,485
‎It's no use!

135
00:11:35,486 --> 00:11:38,655
‎Hand over the corpse in your left arm.

136
00:11:38,656 --> 00:11:41,950
‎I knew it. You were after it all along.

137
00:11:41,951 --> 00:11:43,910
‎Right now!

138
00:11:43,911 --> 00:11:46,371
‎Or do you want to see these rocks

139
00:11:46,372 --> 00:11:50,126
‎spill Gyro's guts all over the place?

140
00:11:58,801 --> 00:11:59,969
‎Gyro!

141
00:12:01,095 --> 00:12:03,472
‎Ka-clang. Ka-clang.

142
00:12:04,682 --> 00:12:08,059
‎Shoot again! Kill Gyro!

143
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:10,020
‎You bastard!

144
00:12:11,647 --> 00:12:12,730
‎Gyro!

145
00:12:12,731 --> 00:12:15,024
‎You can't do a damn thing now!

146
00:12:15,025 --> 00:12:18,027
‎Hand over the corpse already!

147
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:19,321
‎The corpse?

148
00:12:19,864 --> 00:12:22,825
‎Johnny, what corpse?

149
00:12:24,201 --> 00:12:27,371
‎I don't want to give it up.
‎I don't want to.

150
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:29,999
‎What's inside my left arm...

151
00:12:30,958 --> 00:12:33,835
‎My legs can move.

152
00:12:33,836 --> 00:12:35,838
‎Gyro. You saw it, didn't you?

153
00:12:36,338 --> 00:12:39,800
‎My legs... They can move.

154
00:12:42,678 --> 00:12:44,430
‎I was grateful.

155
00:12:45,306 --> 00:12:48,058
‎I was grateful I'd entered the race.

156
00:12:48,934 --> 00:12:54,148
‎Finding this left arm made me feel like
‎I could die without regrets.

157
00:12:54,899 --> 00:12:56,816
‎I don't want to give it up.

158
00:12:56,817 --> 00:13:02,031
‎Someone as insignificant as me
‎finally found a reason to live.

159
00:13:02,573 --> 00:13:04,450
‎I was truly grateful.

160
00:13:07,870 --> 00:13:11,039
‎You've been carrying it all this way?

161
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:13,708
‎Hand it over already!

162
00:13:13,709 --> 00:13:18,296
‎Then I guess it's my job to take him down.

163
00:13:18,297 --> 00:13:20,340
‎What are you babbling about?

164
00:13:20,341 --> 00:13:24,678
‎Go right through Gyro
‎and come to me, Jyohnee!

165
00:13:27,806 --> 00:13:30,475
‎It's over!

166
00:13:30,476 --> 00:13:34,730
‎You tore Gyro apart yourself!

167
00:13:38,651 --> 00:13:40,402
‎He pulled it out?

168
00:13:43,906 --> 00:13:46,408
‎Stop... Just take it.

169
00:13:47,284 --> 00:13:51,663
‎But first, get those hooks out of Gyro.

170
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:54,916
‎Or I'll smash this left arm

171
00:13:54,917 --> 00:13:57,669
‎to pieces myself.

172
00:13:57,670 --> 00:13:59,255
‎Don't!

173
00:14:02,675 --> 00:14:04,176
‎Yes!

174
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:06,678
‎So this is the corpse?

175
00:14:06,679 --> 00:14:10,099
‎I don't get
‎why everyone's after this thing.

176
00:14:10,849 --> 00:14:12,850
‎I'm unbeatable!

177
00:14:12,851 --> 00:14:15,895
‎This proves I'm unbeatable
‎and that I'm smart.

178
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:17,730
‎Now everyone will acknowledge me!

179
00:14:17,731 --> 00:14:21,569
‎Now I can finally work my way to the top!

180
00:14:25,197 --> 00:14:28,491
‎My nails stopped spinning...

181
00:14:28,492 --> 00:14:30,077
‎I can't spin them anymore.

182
00:14:30,661 --> 00:14:33,873
‎My ability is gone.

183
00:14:36,667 --> 00:14:38,251
‎I've got it!

184
00:14:38,252 --> 00:14:40,587
‎Now all that's left is for you two to die!

185
00:14:40,588 --> 00:14:44,173
‎I still haven't gotten
‎those hooks off Gyro!

186
00:14:44,174 --> 00:14:46,885
‎Your nails won't spin?

187
00:14:46,886 --> 00:14:50,305
‎Johnny. They're still spinning.

188
00:14:50,306 --> 00:14:51,849
‎They're still in motion.

189
00:14:55,144 --> 00:14:59,607
‎I got them spinning. Those...

190
00:15:01,692 --> 00:15:03,569
‎The corpse's nails!

191
00:15:08,157 --> 00:15:09,199
‎Told you so.

192
00:15:10,075 --> 00:15:12,536
‎It was my job to take him down.

193
00:15:31,221 --> 00:15:32,181
‎Here.

194
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:36,101
‎You're giving it back? To me?

195
00:15:36,644 --> 00:15:39,687
‎So you didn't know?

196
00:15:39,688 --> 00:15:44,777
‎You mean you didn't enter this race
‎to find the corpse?

197
00:15:45,361 --> 00:15:46,861
‎I'm not interested.

198
00:15:46,862 --> 00:15:49,197
‎Well, maybe a little.

199
00:15:49,198 --> 00:15:51,366
‎Nah, not really.

200
00:15:51,367 --> 00:15:54,577
‎My goal is simply to finish this race
‎in first place.

201
00:15:54,578 --> 00:15:55,955
‎And then...

202
00:16:00,668 --> 00:16:03,294
‎But I'm starting to see what's going on.

203
00:16:03,295 --> 00:16:05,088
‎Looks like those terrorists

204
00:16:05,089 --> 00:16:08,633
‎think I'm hiding the corpse.

205
00:16:08,634 --> 00:16:12,888
‎This isn't the only piece.
‎The corpse is scattered.

206
00:16:13,389 --> 00:16:17,017
‎They're using the Steel Ball Run race
‎to gather them.

207
00:16:17,601 --> 00:16:18,685
‎Why?

208
00:16:18,686 --> 00:16:21,729
‎The left arm alone gave me this power.

209
00:16:21,730 --> 00:16:27,318
‎Isn't it only natural to think
‎the rest would grant even greater power?

210
00:16:27,319 --> 00:16:30,780
‎Come on. Do you realize
‎how huge this continent is?

211
00:16:30,781 --> 00:16:32,407
‎How will you find them?

212
00:16:32,408 --> 00:16:37,037
‎What if they choose their owners
‎the way this one chose me?

213
00:16:37,621 --> 00:16:40,331
‎There's no doubt
‎the corpse has a will of its own.

214
00:16:40,332 --> 00:16:41,958
‎I see.

215
00:16:41,959 --> 00:16:44,210
‎There are thousands of competitors.

216
00:16:44,211 --> 00:16:46,629
‎So they're playing the odds.

217
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:50,299
‎Gyro, I'm sorry
‎I kept the corpse a secret from you,

218
00:16:50,300 --> 00:16:52,010
‎but I want your opinion.

219
00:16:52,011 --> 00:16:55,596
‎What do you think? Whose corpse is it?

220
00:16:55,597 --> 00:17:00,185
‎Hold it. Have you already decided
‎to collect the rest?

221
00:17:00,769 --> 00:17:03,271
‎Yeah. I've already made up my mind.

222
00:17:03,272 --> 00:17:06,941
‎If I give this up, I'll go back
‎to being nothing but a loser.

223
00:17:06,942 --> 00:17:08,110
‎In more ways than one.

224
00:17:08,902 --> 00:17:12,196
‎I'm not going back
‎to being a damn quitter.

225
00:17:12,197 --> 00:17:13,782
‎I'll see it through!

226
00:17:15,534 --> 00:17:18,870
‎Just so we're clear, don't count on me.

227
00:17:18,871 --> 00:17:20,831
‎I'm not collecting corpse parts.

228
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:25,209
‎That said, this is only my opinion.

229
00:17:25,210 --> 00:17:28,296
‎If terrorists
‎are searching for a mummified corpse,

230
00:17:28,297 --> 00:17:30,674
‎there must be some record of it.

231
00:17:31,383 --> 00:17:34,053
‎It's probably the remains of some saint.

232
00:17:34,887 --> 00:17:38,097
‎Gyro! You do know something, don't you?

233
00:17:38,098 --> 00:17:40,099
‎Calm down already!

234
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:42,769
‎I told you this was just my own opinion!

235
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:46,523
‎You're the type who hears half the story
‎and judges others.

236
00:17:47,733 --> 00:17:49,484
‎Movēre Crūs.

237
00:17:49,485 --> 00:17:53,030
‎It's Latin. It means, "Move your legs."

238
00:17:53,739 --> 00:17:55,114
‎Latin?

239
00:17:55,115 --> 00:17:59,495
‎Do you know what makes someone a saint?

240
00:18:00,412 --> 00:18:02,956
‎Like the Virgin Mary or Saint Peter?

241
00:18:03,582 --> 00:18:07,586
‎A saint is someone
‎who performs miracles after death.

242
00:18:08,378 --> 00:18:10,254
‎Listen. I'll say it again.

243
00:18:10,255 --> 00:18:11,881
‎After they're dead.

244
00:18:11,882 --> 00:18:14,884
‎That's how the Vatican defines a saint.

245
00:18:14,885 --> 00:18:19,723
‎A saint must have at least
‎two posthumous miracles.

246
00:18:20,516 --> 00:18:23,226
‎A saint's remains don't decay
‎for centuries,

247
00:18:23,227 --> 00:18:25,019
‎and their power is immense.

248
00:18:25,020 --> 00:18:28,481
‎The only two states to have prospered
‎for over a thousand years

249
00:18:28,482 --> 00:18:30,525
‎are Venice and the Vatican.

250
00:18:30,526 --> 00:18:33,654
‎They say it's because
‎each possesses a saint's remains.

251
00:18:34,404 --> 00:18:37,658
‎A thousand years
‎of promised glory and power.

252
00:18:38,158 --> 00:18:42,203
‎In that case, any nation would want it.

253
00:18:42,204 --> 00:18:43,539
‎And if it were

254
00:18:44,623 --> 00:18:47,709
‎something greater than even a saint...

255
00:18:49,962 --> 00:18:51,504
‎It couldn't be...

256
00:18:51,505 --> 00:18:53,632
‎A saint?

257
00:18:54,466 --> 00:18:58,636
‎The nails spun.
‎My legs moved when they couldn't before.

258
00:18:58,637 --> 00:19:01,639
‎That makes two miracles already.

259
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:06,018
‎Do that in the Vatican, and that mummy
‎would be canonized on the spot.

260
00:19:06,019 --> 00:19:09,105
‎But wait. This is the New World!

261
00:19:09,106 --> 00:19:11,524
‎Has a saint ever even made it to America?

262
00:19:11,525 --> 00:19:13,734
‎And why is it scattered across the land?

263
00:19:13,735 --> 00:19:17,405
‎Have someone back home look into it.
‎They'll find the answer.

264
00:19:17,406 --> 00:19:20,741
‎Saints exist for the sake of others.

265
00:19:20,742 --> 00:19:24,328
‎They don't just disappear
‎into the pages of history.

266
00:19:24,329 --> 00:19:26,080
‎There are bound to be records.

267
00:19:26,081 --> 00:19:30,668
‎What I'm saying is, if you want to collect
‎the corpse, that's your business.

268
00:19:30,669 --> 00:19:34,130
‎But in this race, I finish first.

269
00:19:34,131 --> 00:19:37,342
‎You finish second. Don't forget our deal.

270
00:19:38,135 --> 00:19:40,261
‎In that case, Johnny,

271
00:19:40,262 --> 00:19:42,931
‎I'll let you come with me.

272
00:19:45,350 --> 00:19:50,397
‎Let's go! To Monument Valley
‎and the third stage!

273
00:19:56,111 --> 00:19:57,570
‎That's...

274
00:19:57,571 --> 00:20:00,115
‎Johnny, hurry! It's Dio and Sand Man!

275
00:20:02,075 --> 00:20:04,493
‎Here they come! Second-stage finish!

276
00:20:04,494 --> 00:20:06,495
‎Here in Monument Valley,

277
00:20:06,496 --> 00:20:10,876
‎crowds have gathered
‎to witness the outcome.

278
00:20:11,376 --> 00:20:13,044
‎Diego's in the lead.

279
00:20:13,045 --> 00:20:15,254
‎Behind him, Sand Man. Then Gyro Zeppeli.

280
00:20:15,255 --> 00:20:18,508
‎And Johnny Joestar,
‎who finished fifth in the first stage.

281
00:20:19,009 --> 00:20:22,553
‎Day 18. 750 miles since the start.

282
00:20:22,554 --> 00:20:24,597
‎And as they reach Monument Valley,

283
00:20:24,598 --> 00:20:28,059
‎it's the frontrunners who've pulled ahead.

284
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:30,978
‎Gyro makes his move! 600 yards to go!

285
00:20:30,979 --> 00:20:33,231
‎Diego Brando is picking up speed!

286
00:20:33,232 --> 00:20:36,235
‎Sand Man bounds across the desert
‎with incredible speed!

287
00:20:38,278 --> 00:20:39,403
‎This is...

288
00:20:39,404 --> 00:20:41,989
‎Oh, right. So that's...

289
00:20:41,990 --> 00:20:43,908
‎Gyro! Hey, look!

290
00:20:43,909 --> 00:20:47,119
‎We can win this, Johnny.
‎This stage is ours!

291
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:50,039
‎Keep it wide open!

292
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:51,832
‎That's not it. I figured it out.

293
00:20:51,833 --> 00:20:53,084
‎The arm symbols...

294
00:20:53,085 --> 00:20:54,836
‎-Where the next piece is!
‎-What?

295
00:20:55,379 --> 00:20:56,879
‎They're across the line!

296
00:20:56,880 --> 00:20:59,840
‎Diego Brando takes first.
‎Johnny Joestar finishes second.

297
00:20:59,841 --> 00:21:02,928
‎Sand Man comes in third.
‎Gyro Zeppeli finishes fourth.

298
00:21:04,179 --> 00:21:08,266
‎What're you talking about?
‎Why'd you cross the finish line before me?

299
00:21:08,267 --> 00:21:10,435
‎Wait... No, hold on!

300
00:21:11,103 --> 00:21:12,228
‎Hey, Johnny!

301
00:21:12,229 --> 00:21:14,731
‎Get back here, you bastard!

302
00:21:17,150 --> 00:21:18,359
‎What's this?

303
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:22,154
‎Don't you see? It's a photograph
‎of the third stage course.

304
00:21:22,155 --> 00:21:24,533
‎That mountain has the same shape.

305
00:21:26,576 --> 00:21:28,828
‎These marks aren't letters.

306
00:21:28,829 --> 00:21:32,249
‎They point to a place.
‎They're telling us to go there.

307
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:36,545
‎I'm sure the next piece
‎is on that mountain.

308
00:21:40,090 --> 00:21:44,051
‎Bamboo Hat Kid was found collapsed,
‎clutching this cloth.

309
00:21:44,052 --> 00:21:49,515
‎For some reason, it's scorched like this.
‎The Latin reads, "Move your legs."

310
00:21:49,516 --> 00:21:53,728
‎From the evidence at the scene,
‎it appears the one carrying the corpse

311
00:21:53,729 --> 00:21:56,022
‎is Johnny Joestar, not Gyro.

312
00:21:56,023 --> 00:21:58,567
‎We don't know which piece they found.

313
00:21:59,776 --> 00:22:01,569
‎-The arm.
‎-Sir?

314
00:22:01,570 --> 00:22:03,112
‎Listen carefully.

315
00:22:03,113 --> 00:22:07,658
‎Bamboo Hat Kid
‎wrapped the corpse in this cloth.

316
00:22:07,659 --> 00:22:08,702
‎Like this.

317
00:22:09,369 --> 00:22:12,997
‎Judging by its thickness,
‎it can only be an arm.

318
00:22:12,998 --> 00:22:15,541
‎That's when the cloth was scorched

319
00:22:15,542 --> 00:22:17,669
‎by the energy the corpse gives off.

320
00:22:18,253 --> 00:22:21,088
‎That's something
‎only those remains could do.

321
00:22:21,089 --> 00:22:23,507
‎And these aren't letters.

322
00:22:23,508 --> 00:22:26,470
‎Could they be a message
‎pointing to a location?

323
00:22:27,262 --> 00:22:29,221
‎I've always believed so.

324
00:22:29,222 --> 00:22:33,434
‎But I've never understood
‎what the letters mean.

325
00:22:33,435 --> 00:22:36,688
‎I've thought about it constantly.

326
00:22:37,355 --> 00:22:40,066
‎According to Joseph of Arimathea's map,

327
00:22:40,067 --> 00:22:44,488
‎the remains were divided into nine parts
‎and scattered across the land.

328
00:22:44,988 --> 00:22:47,198
‎That makes two pieces we've found.

329
00:22:47,199 --> 00:22:50,535
‎Including the heart within my body.

330
00:23:06,051 --> 00:23:08,887
‎That just now... His chest...

331
00:23:09,763 --> 00:23:14,850
‎Subtitle translation by: Ryoko Quirke

332
00:23:14,851 --> 00:23:18,271
‎The third stage is about to begin!

333
00:23:18,396 --> 00:23:22,566
‎With such a long stage ahead,
‎stamina matters more than speed!

334
00:23:22,567 --> 00:23:25,987
‎Because of that,
‎we're in for a relatively cautious start.

335
00:23:26,530 --> 00:23:28,114
‎Gyro Zeppeli...

336
00:23:28,115 --> 00:23:31,451
‎There's nothing I can do to help you.

337
00:23:32,536 --> 00:23:34,454
‎They're off!
